module std where

-- not — logical negation. Boolean → Boolean.
--
-- The clause LHS is the bare `not` (id `std:not`).
-- Phase 5b7's `notFn` divergence + the std.ts
-- `f.id === "std-not:notFn"` extraction seam are
-- RETIRED by the word-operator de-reservation
-- precursor (`5121c5b8`, ahead of FM-retire-9 9a),
-- which made `not` an ordinary ident. No `@codeName`.
--
-- Pre-5b7 the spec was TS-native via `stdNatives.not
-- = (x) => !x` at engine/src/modules/std.ts:3207.
-- Post-5b7 the spec gains a body and the
-- `stdNatives.not` entry is deleted. Hybrid of the
-- 5b1-5b4 TS-native-deletion category and the 5b6
-- name-divergence workaround category — first sub-
-- phase combining both.
--
-- Body lowers to canonical if-form `{if: [{var:
-- "x"}, {construct: ["False"]}, {construct:
-- ["True"]}]}`. Engine's `construct` op coerces
-- `True` / `False` constructor refs to JS booleans
-- per AGENTS.md "Bool = True | False", so the
-- runtime VALUE is a JS bool (matching the pre-5b7
-- TS native's `!x` return shape).
--
-- If-lowering source-of-truth migration (5b5 piloted
-- on min/max numeric comparators; 5b6 extended to
-- Boolean short-circuit and/or; 5b7 to Boolean
-- negation). The named-op-key-style dispatch path
-- (via `stdNatives`) is retired for this spec; Bool-
-- negation calls dispatch through the function
-- registry to the if-form body.

@label "Not"
@description "Logical negation — body is `if x then False else True` via if-lowering (Phase 5b7)."
@tags "boolean"
not : (x: Boolean) -> Boolean
not x = if x then False else True
